2","usage":{"input":133,"output":474,"cacheRead":75392,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1,"totalTokens":75999,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784971004524,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-8a83f3e2-4ed9-411f-b191-db61611eee4d","responseModel":"z-ai/glm-5.2"}}
{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The exercise is complete. Summary of what was accomplished:\n\n## Final State\n\n**`src/game-of-life.ts`** — Implements the real Game of Life algorithm:\n- Sparse representation using a `Set` of live cells and a `Map` of live-neighbor counts\n- Handles the infinite grid via the Moore neighborhood (8 neighbor offsets)\n- Applies all four rules: underpopulation (<2 dies), survival (2-3 lives), overpopulation (>3 dies), reproduction (dead cell with exactly 3 born)\n- Handles negative coordinates natively (keys are coordinate strings)\n- Exports `nextGeneration(cells: Cell[]): Cell[]` matching the required API contract\n\n**`src/game-of-life.spec.ts`** — 9 tests, all passing, covering every rule and spec example.\n\n## TDD Workflow Executed\n\n| # | Test | Phase | Outcome |\n|---|------|-------|---------|\n| 1 | Empty input → `[]` | Red→Green→Refactor | ✓ |\n| 2 | Single cell dies (Rule 1) | Red (already passes) | ✓ skipped |\n| 3 | Two adjacent die (Rule 1) | Red (already passes) | ✓ skipped |\n| 4 | L-shape → block (Rule 4) | Red→Green→Refactor | ✓ |\n| 5 | Block still-life (Rule 2) | Red→Green→Refactor | ✓ |\n| 6 | Blinker vertical → horizontal | Red→Green→Refactor | ✓ |\n| 7 | Overpopulation plus → ring (Rule 3) | Red→Green→Refactor | ✓ |\n| 8 | Negative coordinates | Red→Green→Refactor | ✓ |\n| 9 | Blinker 2-generation cycle | Red→Green→Refactor | ✓ |\n\nThe refactor subagents progressively improved the code: extracting constants, consolidating branches, introducing a data-driven lookup table, then a `Map`+`patternKey` for O(1) lookup, and finally — once all tests were green — replacing the hardcoded lookup table with the real neighbor-counting algorithm (the major generalization, removing all conceptual duplication of the rules). All 9 tests pass, `tsc` is clean, and `experiment-done.txt` contains `DONE`."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/glm-5.2",