tical blinker to horizontal -- [(0,0),(0,1),(0,2)] -> [(-1,1),(0,1),(1,1)]\");\n  it.todo(\"should kill a cell with 4 neighbors (Rule 3 overpopulation) -- plus shape -> ring with hollow center\");\n  it.todo(\"should handle negative coordinates -- blinker at [(-2,-1),(-2,0),(-2,1)] -> [(-3,0),(-2,0),(-1,0)]\");\n  it.todo(\"should return a blinker to its original state after 2 generations (full oscillator cycle)\");\n});\n```\n\nGood. Now let me start executing. First, write the test file. Then proceed to Red phase for test 1.\n\nWait — the workflow says read each SKILL before first use. I've read test-list, red, green skills already. Good. I'll follow them.\n\nLet me also reconsider the test comparison helper for when tests become active. I'll add a `sortCells` helper in the test file (defined at top, used in active tests). For it.todo tests, it's not used yet. I'll add it when I activate the first test. Actually, I can include it from the start (it's just a helper). But to keep test-list minimal (it.todo only), maybe add helper when first test activates. I'll add it in the Red phase for test 1.\n\nHmm, the test-list skill says \"Use it.todo() for all tests\" and the template is minimal. I'll keep the test file to just it.todo entries now, and add the helper + active test code in Red phases.\n\nLet me write the test list file now.\n\nThen produce the ## Test List marker and summary, then immediately continue to Red phase (read red skill — already read), produce ## Red for test 1.\n\nLet me write the file.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"I've read the prompt, project setup, and all three skill files. Dependencies are now installed. Let me verify the refactor agent and then begin the TDD workflow with the Test List Phase."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_12b956ce5a17425aad215b06","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_09-00-47_game-of-life-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_glm